@startuml
title MEDORA -- Validate and Issue Prescription (System Sequence)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam dpi 192
skinparam backgroundColor #F5F9FE
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontColor #183247
skinparam defaultFontSize 16
skinparam titleFontSize 20
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #EAF3FB
  BorderColor #2563A6
  FontColor #183247
}
skinparam ArrowColor #2563A6
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF3FB
  ParticipantBorderColor #163A5F
  ParticipantFontColor #183247
  LifeLineBorderColor #2563A6
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F5F9FE
}
actor Doctor
participant "MEDORA System" as System

Doctor -> System: Submit prescription draft and directions
activate System
alt Required data invalid
  System --> Doctor: Reject issue; keep draft unchanged
else Safety warning raised
  System --> Doctor: Show warning and reason
  alt Doctor does not proceed
    Doctor -> System: Retain draft
    System --> Doctor: Confirm not issued
  else Override is permitted and justified
    Doctor -> System: Confirm override(reason)
    System --> Doctor: Return issued prescription reference
  end
else No blocking warning
  System --> Doctor: Return issued prescription reference
end
deactivate System
note over Doctor, System
  Issuing a prescription does not create a dispensing or
  medication-administration event.
end note
@enduml